<!-- ═══════════════════ CHAPTER 1 ═══════════════════ -->
<h1>1. Executive Summary</h1>
<p>The <b>Paperless SOET — Faculty Workload Management System (FWMS)</b> is a full-stack web application built for MGM University's School of Engineering and Technology. The platform digitises the entire lifecycle of academic teaching workload management — from defining institutional hierarchies and configuring workload norms, through assigning faculty to subjects/classes/batches, computing weekly teaching hours automatically, enforcing conflict detection and norm compliance, managing multi-level approval workflows, to generating printable workload distribution reports.</p>

<p>The system serves three user roles — <b>Super Admin</b>, <b>Department Admin (HOD)</b>, and <b>Faculty</b> — each with a tailored dashboard providing real-time analytics on workload distribution. A standout feature is the integration of <b>Google Gemini 2.5 Flash AI</b> for ingesting physical (scanned or photographed) teaching workload spreadsheets, extracting tabular data via multimodal vision, and converting them into structured digital records.</p>

<!-- ═══════════════════ CHAPTER 2 ═══════════════════ -->
<h1>2. Problem Statement &amp; Objectives</h1>

<h2>2.1 Problem Statement</h2>
<p>Traditional university workload distribution relies on paper-based spreadsheets circulated manually between department heads, deans, and administration. This process suffers from:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Manual calculation errors in teaching hours and credit allocations</li>
  <li>No real-time visibility into faculty overload/underload conditions</li>
  <li>Duplicate or conflicting subject-class-faculty assignments across departments</li>
  <li>Delayed approval cycles with no audit trail</li>
  <li>Difficulty producing consolidated reports across multiple departments</li>
  <li>No mechanism to enforce UGC workload norms programmatically</li>
</ul>

<h2>2.2 Objectives</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Automate the computation of weekly teaching hours using configurable multipliers</li>
  <li>Enforce UGC workload norms per designation with overload/underload detection</li>
  <li>Prevent double-booking of class divisions and laboratory batches</li>
  <li>Implement a multi-level approval workflow with SLA-based escalation</li>
  <li>Provide role-specific analytical dashboards with real-time metrics</li>
  <li>Enable AI-powered extraction of data from physical workload documents</li>
  <li>Generate comprehensive, printable workload reports per department per term</li>
  <li>Maintain a complete audit trail of every change and decision</li>
</ol>

