  <tr><td>/dashboard</td><td>Dashboard</td><td>All</td><td>Role-specific analytics dashboard (SuperAdmin/HOD/Faculty)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/institutional</td><td>Institutional Config</td><td>SA</td><td>Manage schools, departments, academic terms, norms</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/master-data</td><td>Master Data</td><td>SA, HOD</td><td>Manage subjects, classes, batches, student strength</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/subjects</td><td>Subjects &amp; Classes</td><td>SA, HOD</td><td>Subject and class management views</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/allocations</td><td>Allocations</td><td>All</td><td>View/create/edit faculty-subject allocations</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/approvals</td><td>Approvals</td><td>SA, HOD</td><td>Review and decide on pending approval requests</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/faculty</td><td>Faculty Management</td><td>SA, HOD</td><td>Create, edit, activate/deactivate faculty accounts</td></tr>
  <tr><td>/workload-report</td><td>Workload Report</td><td>SA, HOD</td><td>Generate, edit, print, and AI-ingest workload reports</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>9.3 Layout Structure</h2>
<p>The protected layout features:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Collapsible Sidebar</b> with a Carbon (#202020) header displaying "FWMS Portal", role-filtered navigation links with Lucide icons, active-state indicators (Signal Orange dot), and a user profile section with sign-out</li>
  <li><b>Top Bar</b> with a mobile hamburger menu toggle and "Paperless SOET" branding</li>
  <li><b>Content Area</b> with a max-width container, entry animation (fade-in + slide-up), and scroll containment</li>
</ul>

<!-- ═══════════════════ CHAPTER 10 ═══════════════════ -->
<h1>10. UI/UX Design System</h1>
<p>The application follows the <b>"Ventriloc"</b> design specification — a professional, data-first aesthetic inspired by modern analytics dashboards.</p>

<h2>10.1 Colour Palette</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Token</th><th>Hex</th><th>Role</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Signal Orange</td><td style="background:#ff682c;color:white;font-weight:bold">#ff682c</td><td>Brand accent — charts, active indicators, overload alerts</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Sienna Bronze</td><td style="background:#816729;color:white">#816729</td><td>Muted secondary brand tone</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Carbon</td><td style="background:#202020;color:white">#202020</td><td>Primary text, button backgrounds, headings</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Graphite</td><td style="background:#4d4d4d;color:white">#4d4d4d</td><td>Secondary text, body emphasis</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Slate</td><td style="background:#828282;color:white">#828282</td><td>Helper text, placeholders, inactive elements</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Fog</td><td style="background:#f5f5f5">#f5f5f5</td><td>Subtle surface tint, hover washes</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Mist</td><td style="background:#efefef">#efefef</td><td>Page canvas / background</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Chalk</td><td style="background:#e8e8e8">#e8e8e8</td><td>Borders, dividers, nav background</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Paper</td><td style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e8e8e8">#ffffff</td><td>Card surfaces, content panels</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>10.2 Typography</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Font</th><th>Usage</th><th>Weights</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Space Grotesk (substitute for PolySans)</td><td>Headings, display text, KPI values</td><td>400, 500, 600</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Inter</td><td>Body text, UI labels, buttons, form elements</td><td>400, 500, 600</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>10.3 Border Radius System</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Element</th><th>Radius</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Cards, Inputs</td><td>8px</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Buttons, Tags</td><td>20px (pill shape)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Navigation Capsule</td><td>200px (full rounded)</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>10.4 Glassmorphism</h2>
<p>A <code>.glass</code> CSS utility class provides a frosted-glass effect: <code>background: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); backdrop-filter: blur(12px);</code> — used on modal overlays like the forced password change screen.</p>

<!-- ═══════════════════ CHAPTER 11 ═══════════════════ -->
<h1>11. Validation &amp; Error Handling</h1>

<h2>11.1 Input Validation (Zod)</h2>
<p>All API request bodies are validated using Zod schemas before reaching the service layer. Validation failures return a <code>400 VALIDATION_ERROR</code> with field-level error details:</p>
<div class="code-block">{
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Invalid request data",
    "details": [
      { "field": "email", "message": "Invalid email format" },
      { "field": "creditHours", "message": "Credit hours must be > 0" }
    ]
  }
}</div>

<h2>11.2 Application Errors (ApiError Class)</h2>
<p>A custom <code>ApiError</code> class provides factory methods for consistent HTTP error responses:</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>Factory Method</th><th>HTTP Status</th><th>Error Code</th></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.badRequest()</td><td>400</td><td>BAD_REQUEST</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.unauthorized()</td><td>401</td><td>UNAUTHORIZED</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.forbidden()</td><td>403</td><td>FORBIDDEN</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.notFound()</td><td>404</td><td>NOT_FOUND</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.conflict()</td><td>409</td><td>CONFLICT</td></tr>
  <tr><td>ApiError.internal()</td><td>500</td><td>INTERNAL_ERROR</td></tr>
</table>

<p>A centralised error handler catches all thrown errors, logs unexpected ones via Pino, and suppresses stack traces in production mode.</p>

<!-- ═══════════════════ CHAPTER 12 ═══════════════════ -->
